{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":1,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1499081550,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDU6SXNzdWUyNDAxNDU4MDE=","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1622","origin":"github"},"title":"Move any configuration inheritance into a plugin","message":"Currently we support inheriting aspects of a parent dataset's configuration in the commands `publish` and `create_sibling`. However, there is clearly a need for expanding this functionality (why shouldn't `create` be able to inherit information from a parent ds?). However, this comes at the cost of blowing up the API. Hence I propose to move all related functionality into a dedicated plugin that is capable of pulling down any relevant configuration from a parent ds. Such plugin can be configured to run prior/post any other command.\n\nMoreover, I propose to implement such a command in a way that it can perform its own (iterative, if needed) operations to enable arbitrary maneuvers -- such as always taking the template configuration from the very topmost dataset in a tree, or even a dedicated cfg template -- without having to interact or interfere with the particular nature of recursive processing done inside the actual command.","files":null}]}